{"caveats":[{"caveat_id":"caveat_d2323ad206bc5aae","evidence_ids":["ev_513302b2a42737a2"],"text":"the disassembly not always results in a uniformly disassembled coin cell geometry, which in turn can create issues with half-cell separation and component handling."},{"caveat_id":"caveat_db83df1f030c2088","evidence_ids":["ev_f5d376cf45523064"],"text":"During the charge/discharge cycling of different battery samples, occasional noise can be observed in the 1st and 2nd cycles (Supporting information, Fig. S1 and S2), which originated from the lack of cell resting time before experiments."},{"caveat_id":"caveat_50d6db0e5393442a","evidence_ids":["ev_0bf145c9c4e05359"],"text":"battery sample number 4 experienced a short-circuit during the 3rd discharge process. Therefore, this battery sample was excluded from further evaluation."}],"characterization":[],"evidence":[{"char_end":374,"char_start":187,"chunk_id":"mdchk_0885d8ef29fb894e","document_char_end":17457,"document_char_start":17270,"evidence_id":"ev_6baf3b4adca20db5","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The preparation of the investigated electrolyte systems was made at (25.0 ± 0.1)◦C. This temperature was also kept during all preparatory and characterization steps in the Proteus system.","source_sha256":"2c3fb5bbc54919dd839d7e5a57a93726b7d417bc0af378457b461ef9a0e4ff15"},{"char_end":2627,"char_start":2463,"chunk_id":"mdchk_0885d8ef29fb894e","document_char_end":19710,"document_char_start":19546,"evidence_id":"ev_513302b2a42737a2","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the disassembly not always results in a uniformly disassembled coin cell geometry, which in turn can create issues with half-cell separation and component handling.","source_sha256":"2c3fb5bbc54919dd839d7e5a57a93726b7d417bc0af378457b461ef9a0e4ff15"},{"char_end":114,"char_start":40,"chunk_id":"mdchk_0e8714da456aa819","document_char_end":30223,"document_char_start":30149,"evidence_id":"ev_ae650ba0c6382592","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The galvanostatic cycling was performed using an EmStat4S instru mentation","source_sha256":"e62a41501b7873a661196ca3dc1cf1130bb532e25a6e345558e1bccb939a416c"},{"char_end":314,"char_start":150,"chunk_id":"mdchk_0e8714da456aa819","document_char_end":30423,"document_char_start":30259,"evidence_id":"ev_661934f0ba284f71","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The charge/discharge cycling of all batteries was performed with a constant current of 0.5 mA in the voltage range from 0.01 to 1.00 V, which represents a 10C-rate.","source_sha256":"e62a41501b7873a661196ca3dc1cf1130bb532e25a6e345558e1bccb939a416c"},{"char_end":238,"char_start":0,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5c0a661b00acb5dc","document_char_end":21236,"document_char_start":20998,"evidence_id":"ev_f5d376cf45523064","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"During the charge/discharge cycling of different battery samples, occasional noise can be observed in the 1st and 2nd cycles (Supporting information, Fig. S1 and S2), which originated from the lack of cell resting time before experiments.","source_sha256":"002de8ac949a05a331a2b07ea3e88a9e1ae236279cb1f37c24b936b45dffbb98"},{"char_end":863,"char_start":709,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5c0a661b00acb5dc","document_char_end":21861,"document_char_start":21707,"evidence_id":"ev_0bf145c9c4e05359","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"battery sample number 4 experienced a short-circuit during the 3rd discharge process. Therefore, this battery sample was excluded from further evaluation.","source_sha256":"002de8ac949a05a331a2b07ea3e88a9e1ae236279cb1f37c24b936b45dffbb98"},{"char_end":612,"char_start":420,"chunk_id":"mdchk_92689ed95586b62e","document_char_end":8944,"document_char_start":8752,"evidence_id":"ev_01e17d2905590a4c","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The Eioneus system consists of a platform with coin cell mounting and supply area, crimping and decrimping stations, a potentiostat-based electrochemical evaluation station and a control board","source_sha256":"765e465db86fd73981973ec888ea31fbc51d888035f3ed113875f6d59d27f55a"},{"char_end":347,"char_start":188,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":11246,"document_char_start":11087,"evidence_id":"ev_6e5fe4a9a0b0abe5","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the robotic system starts the fully automated screening cycle. Bar-coded reaction vessels are checked in and fed to the Proteus robot conveyor in tube rackets.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1032,"char_start":836,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":11931,"document_char_start":11735,"evidence_id":"ev_5406932cb8baa928","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Before dispensing the stock solutions, the test tubes are purged with nitrogen gas. Here after, the solutions of A and B are mixed by stirring for a pre-defined time, which was set to about 1 min.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1233,"char_start":1033,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12132,"document_char_start":11932,"evidence_id":"ev_6c79086bf0b88221","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"An analytical chain, utilizing turbidity, controls if a precipitate has formed or not. If precipitation occurs, the screening cycle proceeds with addition of more solvent and repeated turbidity check.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1399,"char_start":1234,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12298,"document_char_start":12133,"evidence_id":"ev_0a244585992a95ab","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"If no precipitation can be detected, the analytical sequence continues to the next step involving Raman spec troscopy for characterisation of the electrolyte system.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1600,"char_start":1400,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12499,"document_char_start":12299,"evidence_id":"ev_66bd4aa647589196","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Subsequently, sampling of 100 μL, 50 μL and 10 μL of the reaction solution is performed onto a 96-well plate at three different positions for further characteri sation, crystallisation and evaluation.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1896,"char_start":1707,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12795,"document_char_start":12606,"evidence_id":"ev_1d09d84d31dbe0ab","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Our initial investigations show that 50 μL is an appropriate electrolyte vol ume. The electrolyte is dispensed directly onto the anode on the half coin cell prepared by the Eioneus systems.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":183,"char_start":46,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":28978,"document_char_start":28841,"evidence_id":"ev_c8fc1d45c925b229","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The electrode materials Li[Mn2O4] (LMO) and V2O5were provided by Sigma Aldrich and used as an active material without further treat ment.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":431,"char_start":237,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29226,"document_char_start":29032,"evidence_id":"ev_3c39b59cd26e7bfb","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the active material was mixed with conductive carbon super C65(MTI Corpora tion) and polyvinylidene fluoride (PVDF, 5 wt% in *N*-methyl-2-pyrroli done, NMP) binder in a weight ratio of 80:10:10.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":317,"char_start":272,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12